<back><div type="verses">
<lg label="2."><l>I, once Thine enemy,</l><l>Was captured, Lord, by Thee;</l><l>Yet Thee I hold, rebelliously,</l><l>As captive unto me.</l></lg>
<lg label="3."><l>Defeated, Lord, by Thee,</l><l>Thy prisoner I’d be.</l><l>Yet when Thou would’st make home in me,</l><l>I oft imprison Thee.</l></lg>
<lg label="4."><l>Though conquered Lord, by Thee,</l><l>My old man liveth still.</l><l>O, come and be my person, Lord,</l><l>In mind, emotion, will.</l></lg>
<lg label="5."><l>Make me a captive, Lord</l><l>And then I shall be free;</l><l>Break through, have Thine own way in me</l><l>For Thine economy.</l></lg>
</div>
</back>
</music></mei>
